#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "004c4177-ca0e-586c-962a-1220b4b64f47" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85d268a4-da68-5461-a5fd-4325487f2486" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319793} {:answer/id #uuid "8e081505-3e87-527d-928a-050077ac043e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319815} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f2b1f8-3c4d-5787-adea-b1ec3788961d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319903} {:answer/id #uuid "dca55a5a-8830-5a03-b9ee-73e0f828dbe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320062} {:answer/id #uuid "fb52be77-be13-5cd3-9f52-a1bc052f07d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb52be77-be13-5cd3-9f52-a1bc052f07d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320148} :answer-field/id #uuid "e593bb99-2134-5208-8b24-97c01ed0e7f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320638}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8505e165-2993-5e50-9039-0c1c0e794caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-35292" :question/problem "Determine the dimension of\n$\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 22 & -44 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{22}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 22 & -44 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321065 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "004c4177-ca0e-586c-962a-1220b4b64f47" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span Using Row Reduction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267fce2f-8f79-53e9-831e-7c2a90e2adc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319510} {:answer/id #uuid "345eb41a-6222-5988-930d-6af162d31248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319552} {:answer/id #uuid "48471577-d3ba-5647-a23c-9be647a9f57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319607} {:answer/id #uuid "96266788-11c1-5a60-bc6e-f7ab6b25cc84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319834} {:answer/id #uuid "a1b8e6ac-3f8b-59ff-9fcc-f59861669f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48471577-d3ba-5647-a23c-9be647a9f57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186319607} :answer-field/id #uuid "eca04464-a958-5b61-98f7-1d33e413d898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186320654}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2a41f8fd-4b7f-554c-b544-a6304735d193" :question/math-academy-id "q-35302" :question/problem "$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\})=$" :question/worked-solution "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & 5 & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{5}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, \n$\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\})=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a5d11c2-4a7c-5fdc-a363-8a87b90db19e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9d9b911-3c3f-58c5-b3b6-d44535560355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119295} {:answer/id #uuid "df4d4fcd-8faf-530e-b415-5c1f3fed2066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119296} {:answer/id #uuid "e52dbb26-c23e-57e3-b4cf-35ee9f0f3f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119297} {:answer/id #uuid "0de4b9c7-15f2-56b8-8c4e-d86894ba45f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119298} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb91a0b-9c2a-5f24-90dc-175b0eb4a659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119299}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0ac61baf-9210-59b4-8248-21725e9864ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119294}] :question/id #uuid "5b165675-1f3d-55a7-a1a0-5f0b3adccb41" :question/math-academy-id "q-79149" :question/problem "Let $v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of $v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}$. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}$ form a basis of $Span{v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}}$\n2. $dim(Span{v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}}) = 3$\n3. $dim(Span{v_{1}, v_{2}, v_{3}, w}) = 4$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a5d11c2-4a7c-5fdc-a363-8a87b90db19e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Dimension of a Span by Inspection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dcdf7ad-dc8c-5b97-9b5e-c7b134b49b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451717} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5f343f-9134-5395-8a95-5714eed53c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451718}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c5f343f-9134-5395-8a95-5714eed53c21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451718} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c5ea2e4-dd11-528a-87f8-7c77094a84a7" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "996635a3-7de7-52e1-9885-d13e9600bdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451719} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9a86f7-257f-52de-b0bc-b84e386c256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf9a86f7-257f-52de-b0bc-b84e386c256a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451720} :answer-field/id #uuid "90409394-7c69-5b92-8b05-88400b81ffd6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ed5a0f9-b208-53b1-948d-e048fe02a61a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451721} {:answer/id #uuid "f080355d-0cd5-5f51-97e4-a3f5a882e7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f080355d-0cd5-5f51-97e4-a3f5a882e7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451722} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5f3fcac-5294-5f8b-8c36-f97bba56f78e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1fa1e936-cb5b-5073-aaa6-f5f5e931fac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-79323" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w}$\n- **II.** $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}})=3$\n- **III.** $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w})=3$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a basis of a vector space $V$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that span $V.$ The dimension of $V$ is the number of vectors in any basis of $V$ (if such a basis exists). \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We are told that $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ This means that $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w}$ is completely spanned by the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ only, and we are told that ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$, and these are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span.Therefore, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}})=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the given span and this basis contains $3$ vectors, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w})=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}]}
